<h1 class="article-title">Caljan Doubles Production Volumes and Expands Its Team in Liepāja</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p>As global demand for advanced cargo-handling technology grows and the e-commerce market continues to expand steadily, conveyor and automation equipment manufacturer Caljan has doubled its production volumes. As its business grows, the company is expanding its team and recruiting production, engineering and quality assurance specialists at various levels.</p><p>These market trends are driving demand for Caljan equipment from both new customers and long-standing strategic partners, including parcel carriers, postal operators, warehousing companies and retail logistics businesses. Growth is evident in Europe and the United States, where the market has recovered and resumed expansion following several months of uncertainty over tariffs.</p><p>The Liepāja plant is the Caljan Group’s largest manufacturing and engineering centre worldwide, covering the entire product life cycle. Work starts with engineering design and detailed drawings and diagrams for each custom-built system, followed by metalworking, welding, assembly, testing and integration into customers’ systems. Nearly 100 new positions have been created this year, and the workforce in Liepāja is now 29% larger than in January.</p><p>“Every week in Liepāja we now produce twice as many telescopic conveyors as at the beginning of the year. We maintain this pace by following one key principle: preserving the reliability, safety and durability of our equipment. That is only possible with a team that works confidently and with professional precision. The work of our specialists has helped strengthen Caljan’s position as a global market leader, producing durable equipment delivered to customers around the world,” says Gatis Dradeika, Caljan’s Managing Director in Latvia.</p><p>Job Opportunities at Caljan’s Manufacturing Plant</p><p>In response to the sharp increase in orders, Caljan has created several new positions and is inviting specialists to join its production, engineering and quality assurance teams. The company is recruiting electricians, assembly workers, welders, painters and warehouse staff, as well as mechanical engineers, quality engineers and quality managers. Caljan currently has approximately 30 open positions in Liepāja.</p><p>“The e-commerce market is expected to maintain a steady average annual growth rate of around 6% <a href="#_ftn1">[1]</a> over the coming years. This means the current increase in activity is not a short-lived demand surge, and we see the growth in our workload as a stable part of the industry’s long-term development,” says Gatis Dradeika.</p><p>Caljan provides employees with a modern, safe and clean working environment, competitive and fair pay, free lunches, health and accident insurance, and other benefits.</p><p>About Caljan</p><p>Caljan is a world-leading manufacturer of telescopic conveyors and automated loose-load handling solutions. It serves customers in Europe, North America, Asia, Africa and Australia. Caljan’s manufacturing and engineering centre in Liepāja has operated since 2006 and is now the company’s largest such facility, employing 255 people. In addition to conveyors, the site develops innovative automation solutions, and the local team actively contributes to global product development and sales support. The company’s management systems are certified to ISO 9001, ISO 14001 and ISO 50001 standards for quality, environmental and energy management.</p></div>
</div>
